{"id": "EUVD-2026-86163", "enisaUuid": "a0468fbf-0a1a-3ab4-958f-a8af51ba379f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/pagemap: dma-unmap pages before handling migration errors\n\ndrm_pagemap_migrate_unmap_pages() relies on the pages array to determine\nwhich pages require DMA unmapping. However,\ndrm_pagemap_migration_unlock_put_pages() clears the array as part of its\ncleanup, leaving drm_pagemap_migrate_unmap_pages() with no valid page\ninformation if it is called afterward.\n\nCall drm_pagemap_migrate_unmap_pages() before\ndrm_pagemap_migration_unlock_put_pages() so the pages array remains\nvalid during DMA unmapping.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:02:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:08:38", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e4331c6644db85bc6ceb470bd84bcf371b6dbfa6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/415f5a755cec5164b149037bf294e270b78d36c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e6372ec2a3990662ae0a67f56ac0aee19848d5b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9hg7-4qcp-5vr8", "CVE-2026-93284"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2f208503-c9ac-3f1c-83d0-0cf9bed87a2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "34c13b50-2f2b-3ede-b46e-d475c19e64ca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f86ad0ed620cb3c91ec7d5468e93ac68d727539d <9e6372ec2a3990662ae0a67f56ac0aee19848d5b"}, {"id": "a7091b28-7b17-36c7-ab0e-740b5d64c283", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "b6bf12d2-49a1-3adf-9754-5447add250af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d5a9ac88-e23f-334b-9f18-ef6a3c11c00e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}, {"id"